  "term": "prochlorperazine",
  "definition": "Prochlorperazine is a synthetic phenothiazine-related drug with antiemetic, antipsychotic, antihistaminic, and anticholinergic effects. It works in part by blocking dopamine D2 receptors in a brain area involved in triggering vomiting and may help prevent chemotherapy-related nausea and vomiting.",
